From 351b15499fa7cf02fc04c742d3681c00f6d162af Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: A2Tools-patch <patch@localhost>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 01:46:36 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Plugins: your own Jellyfin server in the Streams plugin, home
 network only

A plugin with the permission "video" may now list and play what the
player's own Jellyfin server has: a2.video.jellyfin signs in (the user's
name and password; the meter keeps the address, the user and the server's
key in jellyfin.json in its own folder, readable by the player alone, and
never hands the key to the page), reads the user's libraries, Continue
watching, Next up, a search and an item's intro and credits (fixed paths),
the pictures, and tells the server what plays and how far, so Continue
watching and watched are right in every Jellyfin app.

Only a server in the home network: its address must be a private one
(10.x, 172.16-31.x, 192.168.x, 127.x, fc00::/7, fe80::/10) or a local name
(localhost, *.local, *.lan, *.home.arpa, a name without a dot) whose every
address is such a one. Its own client looks up nothing else, takes no
proxy and follows no redirect, so nothing of it reaches the internet.

mpv plays it in the widget as Twitch and YouTube (a2.video.play with
jellyfin, start, title, source, session, audio): the file as it is, or the
server's conversion to a height; the key goes in mpv's request header,
never in the address. New video controls: seek, skip (seconds), audio and
subtitle (a track of the file), subtitleFile (one of the server's); the
plugin hears the position and the length.

The player row: rewind, forward and skip (with its words, "Skip intro"),
and a state may offer its qualities ("original": the file as it is).
